IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 12, SECTIONS 97 TO 102 (returns, further returns, the offence of
-- not furnishing them, and secrecy of returns).  Part ea2.
-- Source text: inputs/EmA1968.txt (a converter rendering, not the official text).
--
-- Notes for the reader.
--   * Section 98(2) (what a requisition may specify) is a power to set the content of a notice and has no function here;
--     section 100 is repealed.
--   * A plain BOOLEAN or NUMBER answer is a date or count comparison and carries no legal "no".

§ `Part 12 -- returns and further returns (ss 97 to 99)`

-- s 97(1): "The Commissioner may, by notification in the Gazette, require any employer or class of employers to
-- forward to the Commissioner at such time or times as may be specified in the notification a return ... and any
-- such employer must furnish the particulars and information so prescribed."
-- src:4000 | 97.—(1) The Commissioner may, by notification in the Gazette,
-- src:4001 | require any employer or class of employers to forward to the
-- src:4002 | Commissioner at such time or times as may be specified in the
-- src:4003 | notification a return in such form or forms as the Commissioner may
-- src:4004 | approve giving the particulars and information prescribed therein,
-- src:4005 | and any such employer must furnish the particulars and information
-- src:4006 | so prescribed.
@ref s 97(1) (src:4000-4006)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has by notification in the Gazette required the employer or the employer's class to forward a return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 97(1) the employer must furnish the particulars and information prescribed in the return` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has by notification in the Gazette required the employer or the employer's class to forward a return`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "any such employer", an employer or class of employers the Commissioner has required by notification to forward a return
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 97(2): "A person is not bound to furnish any particulars or information other than such as are accessible to the
-- person in the course of or derivable from any profession, business, trade or work in the conduct or supervision of
-- which that person is engaged."
-- src:4008 | (2) A person is not bound to furnish any particulars or information
-- src:4009 | other than such as are accessible to the person in the course of or
-- src:4010 | derivable from any profession, business, trade or work in the conduct
-- src:4011 | or supervision of which that person is engaged.
@ref s 97(2) (src:4008-4011)
GIVEN `the particulars or information are accessible to the person in the course of, or derivable from, a profession, business, trade or work in the conduct or supervision of which the person is engaged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 97(2) the person is bound to furnish the particulars or information` MEANS
    IF NOT `the particulars or information are accessible to the person in the course of, or derivable from, a profession, business, trade or work in the conduct or supervision of which the person is engaged`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not bound to furnish any particulars or information other than such as are accessible"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only relieves a person of particulars or information that are not accessible to the person in the course of, or derivable from, the person's profession, business, trade or work
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 98(1): "The Commissioner may give written notice to any employer ... requiring the employer to furnish within a
-- reasonable time stated in the notice fuller or further returns respecting any matter as to which a return is
-- required under this Act or the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990."
-- src:4015 | 98.—(1) The Commissioner may give written notice to any
-- src:4016 | employer, when and as often as the Commissioner thinks
-- src:4017 | necessary, requiring the employer to furnish within a reasonable
-- src:4018 | time stated in the notice fuller or further returns respecting any matter
-- src:4019 | as to which a return is required under this Act or the Employment of
-- src:4020 | Foreign Manpower Act 1990.
@ref s 98(1) (src:4015-4020)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has given the employer written notice requiring it to furnish fuller or further returns within a reasonable time stated in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is one as to which a return is required under this Act or the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(1) the employer is required to furnish the fuller or further returns` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has given the employer written notice requiring it to furnish fuller or further returns within a reasonable time stated in the notice`
       AND `the matter is one as to which a return is required under this Act or the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is by written notice, for fuller or further returns respecting a matter as to which a return is required under this Act or the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 99: "For the purpose of obtaining full information in respect of any employer's employees, the Commissioner may
-- give written notice to such person requiring that person, within the time stated in the notice, to complete and
-- deliver to the Commissioner any return specified in the notice and in addition or alternatively requiring that
-- person to attend personally before the Commissioner or any inspecting officer specified in the notice and to
-- produce for examination any books, documents, accounts and returns which the Commissioner may consider necessary."
-- src:4037 | 99. For the purpose of obtaining full information in respect of any
-- src:4038 | employer’s employees, the Commissioner may give written notice to
-- src:4039 | such person requiring that person, within the time stated in the notice,
-- src:4040 | to complete and deliver to the Commissioner any return specified in
-- src:4041 | the notice and in addition or alternatively requiring that person to
-- src:4042 | attend personally before the Commissioner or any inspecting officer
-- src:4043 | specified in the notice and to produce for examination any books,
-- src:4044 | documents, accounts and returns which the Commissioner may
-- src:4045 | consider necessary.
@ref s 99 (src:4037-4045)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has given the person written notice for the purpose of obtaining full information in respect of an employer's employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 99 the person must complete and deliver the return, or attend and produce the books, documents, accounts and returns, as the notice requires` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has given the person written notice for the purpose of obtaining full information in respect of an employer's employees`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement arises from the Commissioner's written notice given for the purpose of obtaining full information in respect of any employer's employees
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 12 -- the offence of not furnishing returns (s 101)`

-- s 101(1)(a): "wilfully refuses or without lawful excuse (the proof of which is to lie on the employer) neglects to
-- furnish the particulars or information required within the time allowed for furnishing the particulars and
-- information, or to furnish the particulars and information in the form specified or prescribed, or to authenticate
-- the particulars and information at the place or in the manner specified or prescribed".  The proof of lawful excuse
-- lies on the employer: an excuse not proved is no excuse.
-- src:4053 | (a) wilfully refuses or without lawful excuse (the proof of
-- src:4054 | which is to lie on the employer) neglects to furnish the
-- src:4055 | particulars or information required within the time allowed
-- src:4056 | for furnishing the particulars and information, or to furnish
-- src:4057 | the particulars and information in the form specified or
-- src:4058 | prescribed, or to authenticate the particulars and
-- src:4059 | information at the place or in the manner specified or
-- src:4060 | prescribed for the delivery thereof;
@ref s 101(1)(a) (src:4053-4060)
GIVEN `the employer wilfully refused to furnish or to authenticate the particulars or information as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer neglected to furnish or to authenticate the particulars or information as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has proved a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101(1)(a) the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer wilfully refused to furnish or to authenticate the particulars or information as required`
       OR (`the employer neglected to furnish or to authenticate the particulars or information as required` AND (NOT `the employer has proved a lawful excuse`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is of an employer who wilfully refuses, or neglects without a lawful excuse the proof of which is on the employer
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 101(1)(b): "wilfully furnishes or causes to be furnished any false particulars or information in respect of any
-- matter specified in the notice requiring particulars or information to be furnished".
-- src:4062 | (b) wilfully furnishes or causes to be furnished any false
-- src:4063 | particulars or information in respect of any matter
-- src:4064 | specified in the notice requiring particulars or
-- src:4065 | information to be furnished; or
@ref s 101(1)(b) (src:4062-4065)
GIVEN `the employer wilfully furnished or caused to be furnished false particulars or information in respect of a matter specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101(1)(b) the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer wilfully furnished or caused to be furnished false particulars or information in respect of a matter specified in the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is of an employer who wilfully furnishes or causes to be furnished false particulars or information
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 101(1)(c): "refuses to answer, or wilfully gives a false answer to, any question necessary for obtaining any
-- information or particulars required to be furnished under this Act".
-- src:4070 | (c) refuses to answer, or wilfully gives a false answer to, any
-- src:4071 | question necessary for obtaining any information or
-- src:4072 | particulars required to be furnished under this Act,
-- src:4074 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:4075 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:4076 | 6 months or to both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a
-- src:4077 | further fine not exceeding $500 for every day during which the
-- src:4078 | offence continues, and in respect of false particulars, information and
-- src:4079 | answers, the offence is deemed to continue until true particulars,
-- src:4080 | information or answers have been furnished or given.
@ref s 101(1)(c) (src:4070-4080)
GIVEN `the employer refused to answer, or wilfully gave a false answer to, a question necessary for obtaining information or particulars required to be furnished under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101(1)(c) the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer refused to answer, or wilfully gave a false answer to, a question necessary for obtaining information or particulars required to be furnished under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is of an employer who refuses to answer, or wilfully gives a false answer to, such a question
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 101(1): any employer within paragraph (a), (b) or (c) "shall be guilty of an offence".
-- src:4051 | 101.—(1) Any employer who —
@ref s 101(1) (src:4051)
GIVEN `the answer of s 101(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 101(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 101(1)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101(1) the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 101(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 101(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 101(1)(c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is the conduct in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 101(1): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both, and in the
-- case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $500 for every day during which the offence continues".
-- src:4070 | (c) refuses to answer, or wilfully gives a false answer to, any
-- src:4071 | question necessary for obtaining any information or
-- src:4072 | particulars required to be furnished under this Act,
-- src:4074 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:4075 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:4076 | 6 months or to both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a
-- src:4077 | further fine not exceeding $500 for every day during which the
-- src:4078 | offence continues, and in respect of false particulars, information and
-- src:4079 | answers, the offence is deemed to continue until true particulars,
-- src:4080 | information or answers have been furnished or given.
@ref s 101(1) (src:4070-4080)
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 101(1) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    `Penalty on conviction` WITH
        `least fine in dollars` IS 0
        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

-- src:4070 | (c) refuses to answer, or wilfully gives a false answer to, any
-- src:4071 | question necessary for obtaining any information or
-- src:4072 | particulars required to be furnished under this Act,
-- src:4074 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:4075 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:4076 | 6 months or to both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a
-- src:4077 | further fine not exceeding $500 for every day during which the
-- src:4078 | offence continues, and in respect of false particulars, information and
-- src:4079 | answers, the offence is deemed to continue until true particulars,
-- src:4080 | information or answers have been furnished or given.
@ref s 101(1) (src:4070-4080)
GIVEN `the days during which the offence continues` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 101(1) the greatest further fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    max 0 `the days during which the offence continues` TIMES 500

-- s 101(1): "in respect of false particulars, information and answers, the offence is deemed to continue until true
-- particulars, information or answers have been furnished or given."  The days counted run from the day the false
-- particulars were furnished up to, and not including, the day the true ones were furnished (fork F16); until they are,
-- up to and not including the day asked about.
-- src:4070 | (c) refuses to answer, or wilfully gives a false answer to, any
-- src:4071 | question necessary for obtaining any information or
-- src:4072 | particulars required to be furnished under this Act,
-- src:4074 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:4075 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:4076 | 6 months or to both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a
-- src:4077 | further fine not exceeding $500 for every day during which the
-- src:4078 | offence continues, and in respect of false particulars, information and
-- src:4079 | answers, the offence is deemed to continue until true particulars,
-- src:4080 | information or answers have been furnished or given.
@ref s 101(1) (src:4070-4080)
GIVEN `the day the false particulars, information or answers were furnished or given` IS A DATE
      `the day the true particulars, information or answers were furnished or given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the question is asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 101(1) the days a false-particulars offence is deemed to continue` MEANS
    max 0 ((CONSIDER `the day the true particulars, information or answers were furnished or given`
            WHEN JUST truthful THEN truthful
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the question is asked about`) MINUS `the day the false particulars, information or answers were furnished or given`)

-- The "until" bar as its own yes/no question (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05, "does not pass until X" and
-- similar bars; fork F19): the offence is deemed to continue on a day from the day the false particulars
-- were furnished until true ones have been furnished.  TRUE on each day before the day the true ones were
-- furnished, FALSE from that day on.  It never claims that true particulars have been furnished: where the
-- day they were is not given it is TRUE for every day from the false one (the text does not end the offence).
-- src:4070 | (c) refuses to answer, or wilfully gives a false answer to, any
-- src:4071 | question necessary for obtaining any information or
-- src:4072 | particulars required to be furnished under this Act,
-- src:4074 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:4075 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:4076 | 6 months or to both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a
-- src:4077 | further fine not exceeding $500 for every day during which the
-- src:4078 | offence continues, and in respect of false particulars, information and
-- src:4079 | answers, the offence is deemed to continue until true particulars,
-- src:4080 | information or answers have been furnished or given.
@ref s 101(1) (src:4070-4080)
GIVEN `the day the false particulars, information or answers were furnished or given` IS A DATE
      `the day the true particulars, information or answers were furnished or given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101(1) the false-particulars offence is deemed to continue on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the day the false particulars, information or answers were furnished or given`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming runs from the day the false particulars were furnished, and the text says nothing of an earlier day
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the day the true particulars, information or answers were furnished or given`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST truthful THEN
            IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN truthful
            THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offence is deemed to continue until true particulars, information or answers have been furnished or given"
            ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 101(2): "A certificate under the hand of the Commissioner stating that such returns have not been furnished or are
-- incorrect is sufficient prima facie evidence of the truth of the facts stated in the certificate."
-- src:4082 | (2) A certificate under the hand of the Commissioner stating that
-- src:4083 | such returns have not been furnished or are incorrect is sufficient
-- src:4084 | prima facie evidence of the truth of the facts stated in the certificate.
@ref s 101(2) (src:4082-4084)
GIVEN `the certificate is under the hand of the Commissioner and states that the returns have not been furnished or are incorrect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101(2) the certificate is sufficient prima facie evidence of the facts it states` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is under the hand of the Commissioner and states that the returns have not been furnished or are incorrect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a certificate under the hand of the Commissioner stating that returns have not been furnished or are incorrect
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 101(3): "Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to any information furnished or required to be furnished under
-- section 96A by an employer on the retrenchment of any employee by the employer."
-- src:4086 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to any information
-- src:4087 | furnished or required to be furnished under section 96A by an
-- src:4088 | employer on the retrenchment of any employee by the employer.
