`s 101(3) subsections (1) and (2) apply to the information` MEANS
    IF `the information is furnished or required to be furnished under section 96A by an employer on the retrenchment of an employee`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to any information furnished or required to be furnished under"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection takes out only information furnished or required under section 96A on retrenchment
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 12 -- returns not to be published or disclosed (s 102)`

-- s 102(1), first limb: a return or answer "must not, without the previous written consent of the person having the
-- control, management or superintendence of the profession, business, trade or work in relation to which the return or
-- answer was furnished or given, be published".  No person is named as the bearer of this prohibition.
-- src:4094 | 102.—(1) Any return of particulars or information or part of a
-- src:4095 | return furnished, or answer to any question put, for the purposes of
-- src:4096 | this Act must not, without the previous written consent of the person
-- src:4097 | having the control, management or superintendence of the profession,
-- src:4098 | business, trade or work in relation to which the return or answer was
-- src:4099 | furnished or given, be published; and, except for the purposes of a
-- src:4100 | prosecution under this Act, any person not engaged in connection
-- src:4101 | with the collection or preparation of statistics under this Act must not
-- src:4102 | be permitted to see any such individual return or any such part of an
-- src:4103 | individual return.
@ref s 102(1) (src:4094-4103)
GIVEN `the previous written consent of the person having the control, management or superintendence was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(1) the return or answer may be published` MEANS
    IF NOT `the previous written consent of the person having the control, management or superintendence was given`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not, without the previous written consent of the person having the"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection forbids publication without the previous written consent; it never says that publication with it is permitted, so the twin `s 102(1) the return or answer must not be published` below asks the text's own question
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The twin that asks the text's own question, with its own verb ("must not ... be published").  "Without
-- the previous written consent" works as "unless": with the consent the text's answer is no (rulings of
-- 2026-11-05; fork F18).
-- src:4094 | 102.—(1) Any return of particulars or information or part of a
-- src:4095 | return furnished, or answer to any question put, for the purposes of
-- src:4096 | this Act must not, without the previous written consent of the person
