`s 102(1) the person may be permitted to see the individual return` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is engaged in connection with the collection or preparation of statistics under this Act`) AND (NOT `it is for the purposes of a prosecution under this Act`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any person not engaged in connection with the collection or preparation of statistics under this Act must not be permitted"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection forbids permitting a person not so engaged to see the return; it never says that a person so engaged, or a prosecution, is permitted, so the twin `s 102(1) the person must not be permitted to see the individual return` below asks the text's own question
