        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12

-- s 102(3): "In any report, summary of statistics, or other publication prepared under this Act with reference to any
-- trade or industry, the particulars comprised in any return must not be disclosed in any manner whatever, or
-- arranged in any way which would enable any person to identify any particulars so published as being particulars
-- relating to any individual person or business."
-- src:4119 | (3) In any report, summary of statistics, or other publication
-- src:4120 | prepared under this Act with reference to any trade or industry, the
-- src:4121 | particulars comprised in any return must not be disclosed in any
-- src:4122 | manner whatever, or arranged in any way which would enable any
-- src:4123 | person to identify any particulars so published as being particulars
-- src:4124 | relating to any individual person or business.
@ref s 102(3) (src:4119-4124)
GIVEN `the publication discloses the particulars comprised in a return, or arranges them in a way which would enable a person to identify them as relating to an individual person or business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(3) the publication may disclose or arrange the particulars in that way` MEANS
    IF `the publication discloses the particulars comprised in a return, or arranges them in a way which would enable a person to identify them as relating to an individual person or business`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the particulars comprised in any return must not be disclosed in any manner whatever"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection forbids that disclosure and arrangement; it does not say that any other is permitted
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 102(4): "If any person, having possession of any information which to the person's knowledge has been disclosed in
-- contravention of this section, publishes or communicates to any other person any such information, the person shall
-- be guilty of an offence".
