GIVEN `the person has possession of information that to the person's knowledge has been disclosed in contravention of section 102` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes or communicates the information to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person has possession of information that to the person's knowledge has been disclosed in contravention of section 102` AND `the person publishes or communicates the information to another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any person, having possession of any information which to the person's knowledge has been disclosed in"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 102(4) (src:4126-4131)
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 102(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    `Penalty on conviction` WITH
        `least fine in dollars` IS 0
        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12

